meta {
  name: Reschedule Appointment
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/portal/appointments/{{portalAppointmentId}}/reschedule
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Origin: {{portalOrigin}}
  X-CSRF-Token: {{portalCsrfToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "startUtc": "{{slotStartUtc}}",
    "patientTimezone": "America/Bogota"
  }
}

docs {
  Requires the server to run with `ENABLE_SELF_SERVE=true` ("Mis citas" is off by default: every
  /portal path answers 404) and a `portal_session` cookie. No login issues that cookie now that the
  codes are gone, so this request only works against a session minted for a future login.

  Moves one of the session patient's online bookings to `startUtc`, in place (same appointment id).
  Run List Appointments first (it stores `portalAppointmentId`), then Public
  Booking > Get Slots for a free time (it stores `slotStartUtc`). Needs the session cookie, the exact
  Origin and the CSRF token. Reschedule Slots (or Public Booking > Get Slots) stores a free `slotStartUtc`.

  The body is strict: only the new start and the device's IANA zone. The end comes from the type's
  current duration; price, status and confirmation stay as they were. The linked reminder follows
  the new time (cancelled when it is under 24h away; a reminder already sent is kept and a new one
  is linked). Patient and provider are notified with the previous and new times.

  200 `{ appointment }`. 409 "Slot no longer available" (taken, off-grid, outside the window, lead
  time or horizon), 409 "Reschedule unavailable" (a provider-created appointment, or its type or
  location is no longer bookable online), 400 "New time must differ from the current one", 404
  "Appointment not found" (not theirs, unknown, past, cancelled), 404 "Provider not found" when
  booking is off or in approval mode.
}
